**Status** Done on 2026-11-22. The isolated native replay, fresh-process reopen, three timing runs and the fixture and contract checks passed. [November replay, findings and reproduction steps](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/resumption-2026-11-22/README.md)

On 2026-10-25 the native replay passed hit/drag, queued physics controls, matching Area attraction, independent gravity, settling and isolation of a second workspace. The inputs and specification reviews for 01.W02 and 01.W03 also passed. [Completion audit](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/completion-audit.json) · [36 targeted checks and replay attempts](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/verification.json)

The October development run observed a 1920 × 1052 viewport, a manual physics clock and concurrent work. Across 251 frames its p95 interval was 125.54 ms. The single presented-state drag sample was 140.21 ms. Settled idle produced zero native wake signals over 1.531 s while the process used 0.43 CPU-seconds. The optimized 1280 × 720 profile has its own targets. Exact GPU time and total residency were unavailable. [Machine and build](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/build-and-machine.json) · [Raw replay](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/baseline/baseline.json) · [Measurement interpretation](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/baseline/measurement-interpretation.json) · [Governing profile](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/profile.json)

**Current fixture check, 2026-11-22.** Running `target/debug/xtask workspace check institute/fixtures/workspace/stage01/dataset` exited successfully on the current checkout. It inspected 10 cases, five scene roots and 1,636,549 packed bytes. The isolated replay and wall-clock measurements are recorded in the handoff below. [Retained dataset manifest](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/dataset/manifest.json)

## Isolated recheck

- [x] Review changes since the captured build, fixture rights and independent dimensions. Recheck the retained dataset, fixture suite and affected native/engine/transport correctness cases in the repository’s normal interface development environment. Use fresh output directories. Retain the historical artifacts.
- [x] Reserve a machine window free of competing development, builds and tests. Finish compilation before timing. Record current revision and dirty-source or binary hashes, hardware, driver, actual viewport, build profile, instrumentation, remaining OS load, cold/warm state and sample counts.
- [x] Replay 01.W01 through real native input with the documented Area settings. Verify hit identity, drag, queued control, attraction within one canvas unit, independent falling and sleeping, the other workspace’s position and settled idle. Inspect both screenshots, the trace and reopened saved state. Recheck 01.W02/W03 against the retained inputs and contracts. [Fixture and replay settings](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/verification.json) · [Before drag](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/resumption-2026-11-22/before-drag.png) · [After settling](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/resumption-2026-11-22/settled.png)
- [x] Take separate representative active, repeated input and settled-idle timing samples. The supplied correctness harness uses screenshots, a manual clock and one drag. Use or add a narrowly scoped uninstrumented timing mode to the existing native path if needed. Record workload, wall-clock frame intervals, input measurement boundary, count, latency distribution and CPU, memory and available graphics counters. Keep results from different viewports, profiles and instrumentation labeled separately. Record unavailable metrics explicitly.
- [x] Classify the five findings individually as reproduced, not reproduced under recorded conditions, environment-dependent or unresolved. Attach evidence and a next owner to renderer allocation on workspace switch, synthetic Wayland cursor warp, frame/input/idle CPU, overlapping labels and the accessibility D-Bus warning. Repair a failure of the required baseline workflow before advancing. [Historical findings and screenshots](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage01/qualitative-review.json)
- [x] Publish the current run, comparisons and remaining findings in the [baseline handoff](../features/Baseline.lingua#completion-and-handoff) and record its evidence in the [durable model start gate](../features/Model.lingua#start-gate). Stage 002 starts once these results exist.

The existing fixture and replay commands run from the repository root. The last command is the correctness replay. Use the November recipe below for native feature flags, the repeated-input timing run and fresh-process reopen. Choose a fresh leaf directory for each run.

```sh
cargo xtask workspace check institute/fixtures/workspace/stage01/dataset
cargo test --locked -p xtask --features authoring workspace::tests
cargo test --locked -p transport --test workspace_live
cargo test --locked -p engine --test workspace_sync
mkdir -p target/workspace-evidence/stage-001
cargo xtask workspace baseline target/workspace-evidence/stage-001/replay-01
```

The [fixture CLI](../../../../crates/xtask/src/workspace/mod.rs) and [native replay](../../../../crates/sandbox/examples/workspace_baseline.rs) are the starting points for the rerun. Retain the new evidence outside disposable build results before citing it in the handoff.

